From 821018f66193e60ee6861173fbb63cd006d08ad5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jev-router <jev-router@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:10:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(providers): gemini-web mode selection must be
 stale-handle-proof and self-contained in-page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Live testing on the deployed build exposed two bugs in the mode-selection flow:

1. ElementHandle clicks landed on detached nodes: Angular replaces the mode
   picker during hydration, so a handle from before the click is dead by the
   time click() executes — the menu never opens, intermittently (roughly every
   other request under Docker load), surfacing as control_not_found.

2. The in-page pollers referenced a module-scope sleep helper, which
   Playwright cannot serialize into the page — page.evaluate threw
   ReferenceError: sleepInPage is not defined inside the browser, failing
   every mode switch with a 500.

Rewrite the flow around self-contained in-page async pollers: wait-and-click
the picker, wait-and-click the pattern-matching menu item, wait-and-read the
aria-label indicator — all fresh-queried, all serializable, retried up to 3x.
Fail-closed reasons preserved: menu item never lands -> control_not_found;
item landed but never confirmed -> indicator_mismatch.

Unit tests drive the pollers directly with stubbed documents; integration
tests route the three evaluate shapes through the fake page. Verified live:
Argon mode switch confirmed end-to-end on the signed-in account.
